<Routine Name="AUTOLVL" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[WkRoll AutoLvl Control Block]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 4 — ) Assign the program I/O to the following control bits for use by the auto level routine. Set the Permissives for the Auto Level Sequence. )]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(RESET)XIO(M0815)XIC(HYDARUN)XIC(HYDSRUN)XIC(M0813)XIC(M1004)XIC(POLTOUT)XIC(POLBOUT)XIC(ROLLSIN)OTE(CONT_AUTOLVL_4);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 5]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(CONT_AUTOLVL_4)XIC(CTRBLON)XIO(RAILSUP)XIC(BUTKPIN)XIC(BUBKPIN)XIC(WKKPIN)XIC(SPNDOUT)XIC(M0913)XIC(OFFLINE)OTE(M0897);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 6]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(I0834)OTE(M0898);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 7]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(I0615)ONS(OSR_M0919)OTE(M0919);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 8]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(M0919)XIC(M0897)ONS(OSR_M0899)OTE(M0899);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 9 — This bit is here to detect that the work rolls have come together and separating force exists. This will enable the program to jog the mill.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(SDSSR19)OTE(M0900);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 9 — This bit is here to detect that the work rolls have come together and separating force exists. This will enable the program to jog the mill.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(SDSSR19)OTE(Q0907);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 11]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(M0822)OTE(FRNTFRC);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 12]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(M0823)OTE(REARFRC);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 13]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(FRNTFRC)XIO(REARFRC)OTE(FFFB404);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 14]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(FRNTFRC)XIC(REARFRC)OTL(SDFORCE);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 15]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(FRNTFRC)XIO(REARFRC)OTU(SDFORCE);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 16 — The auto level sequence can be aborted in several ways. If the level sequence is active, and the request to begin has already occurred, abort the levelling cycle if the level pushbutton is pressed again. If the permissive is lost or the watchdog timer times out, abort the cycle. If Separating force is detected and the rolls are not turning. If the screwdown board tells us the level is no longer active, abort. This abort can happen at any time during the level cycle. If the drive enable/acknowledge is lost at anytime abort the sequence. The auto level abort is disabled when the level cycle is idle.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(SDFORCE),XIO(WKRLVL0)]XIO(OFFLINE)OTE(Q0905);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 18]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(WKRLVL0),XIO(M0900)XIO(WKRLVL1)XIO(WKRLVL2)XIO(WKRLVL5)XIO(FFFB523)XIO(FFFB525),XIO(WKRLVL1)XIO(WKRLVL5)XIO(M0898)XIO(FFFB523)XIO(FFFB524)XIO(FFFB528),XIC(WKRLVLT),XIO(M0897),XIO(MILLTRN)XIC(M0914)]XIC(M0899)OTL(FFFB523);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
