<![CDATA[[XIC(FFACK5),XIC(M0910)]OTU(FFFB528);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 20 — This auto level reset can be determined in different ways depending on the type of mill. This bit will return control of the mill back to the main program. This bit should be defined as the auto level has finished and the work rolls have come to a complete stop. In some cases it could be a mill jog not active bit or a zero speed signal.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(M0919),XIO(M0900)XIO(WKRLVL1)XIO(WKRLVL2)XIO(WKRLVL5),XIC(WKRLVLT),XIO(M0897),XIO(MILLTRN)XIC(M0914),XIO(M0898)XIO(WKRLVL1)]XIO(WKRLVL0)OTL(WKRLVLA);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 22 — There are a few ways to terminate the auto level cycle but all allow the level cycle to terminate and shut down in normal sequence, such as stopping the mill from jogging, etc. If the cycle is active and the signal from the screwdown board is lost, consider the cycle complete. If the level abort signal is active end the levelling process.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(WKRLVL5)XIO(M0900)XIO(M0898)XIO(MILLTRN)OTE(WKRLVL6);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 22 — There are a few ways to terminate the auto level cycle but all allow the level cycle to terminate and shut down in normal sequence, such as stopping the mill from jogging, etc. If the cycle is active and the signal from the screwdown board is lost, consider the cycle complete. If the level abort signal is active end the levelling process.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(WKRLVL5)XIO(M0900)XIO(M0898)XIO(MILLTRN)OTU(WKRLVLA);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 22 — There are a few ways to terminate the auto level cycle but all allow the level cycle to terminate and shut down in normal sequence, such as stopping the mill from jogging, etc. If the cycle is active and the signal from the screwdown board is lost, consider the cycle complete. If the level abort signal is active end the levelling process.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(WKRLVL5)XIO(M0900)XIO(M0898)XIO(MILLTRN)OTE(FFFB522);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 24 — Once separating force has been detected, preset the watchdog timer. Then wait for the cycle to complete.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(WKRLVL4)XIO(SDFORCE),XIC(WKRLVLA),XIC(WKRLVL5)]XIO(WKRLVL6)OTE(WKRLVL5);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 24 — Once separating force has been detected, preset the watchdog timer. Then wait for the cycle to complete.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(WKRLVL4)XIO(SDFORCE),XIC(WKRLVLA),XIC(WKRLVL5)]XIO(WKRLVL6)OTE(FFFB521);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 26 — When the level request is given wait for the screwdown board to acknowledge the level request. Once the screwdown board says the leveling is active start the sequence and set a watchdog timer to wait for the separating force.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(WKRLVL3)XIC(SDFORCE),XIC(WKRLVL4)]XIO(WKRLVL5)MOV(2400,R00812);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 26 — When the level request is given wait for the screwdown board to acknowledge the level request. Once the screwdown board says the leveling is active start the sequence and set a watchdog timer to wait for the separating force.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(WKRLVL3)XIC(SDFORCE),XIC(WKRLVL4)]XIO(WKRLVL5)OTE(WKRLVL4);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 26 — When the level request is given wait for the screwdown board to acknowledge the level request. Once the screwdown board says the leveling is active start the sequence and set a watchdog timer to wait for the separating force.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(WKRLVL3)XIC(SDFORCE),XIC(WKRLVL4)]XIO(WKRLVL5)OTE(FFFB520);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 28 — When the level request is given wait for the Cegelec to acknowledge the level request. Once the Cegelec acknowledged start the sequence and set a watchdog timer to wait for the screwdown board.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(WKRLVL2)XIC(M0900),XIC(WKRLVL3)]XIO(WKRLVL4)XIO(WKRLVL5)MOV(3600,R00812);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 28 — When the level request is given wait for the Cegelec to acknowledge the level request. Once the Cegelec acknowledged start the sequence and set a watchdog timer to wait for the screwdown board.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(WKRLVL2)XIC(M0900),XIC(WKRLVL3)]XIO(WKRLVL4)XIO(WKRLVL5)OTE(WKRLVL3);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 28 — When the level request is given wait for the Cegelec to acknowledge the level request. Once the Cegelec acknowledged start the sequence and set a watchdog timer to wait for the screwdown board.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(WKRLVL2)XIC(M0900),XIC(WKRLVL3)]XIO(WKRLVL4)XIO(WKRLVL5)OTE(FFFB519);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 30 — When the level cycle is idle, send the auto level request to Cegelec and the screwdown board when the pushbutton is pressed. Set a watchdog timer preset value that will abort the level cycle if the screwdown board does not respond.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(WKRLVL1)XIC(M0898),XIC(WKRLVL2)]XIO(WKRLVL3)XIO(WKRLVL5)MOV(20,R00812);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="38" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 30 — When the level cycle is idle, send the auto level request to Cegelec and the screwdown board when the pushbutton is pressed. Set a watchdog timer preset value that will abort the level cycle if the screwdown board does not respond.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(WKRLVL1)XIC(M0898),XIC(WKRLVL2)]XIO(WKRLVL3)XIO(WKRLVL5)OTE(WKRLVL2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="39" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 30 — When the level cycle is idle, send the auto level request to Cegelec and the screwdown board when the pushbutton is pressed. Set a watchdog timer preset value that will abort the level cycle if the screwdown board does not respond.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(WKRLVL1)XIC(M0898),XIC(WKRLVL2)]XIO(WKRLVL3)XIO(WKRLVL5)OTE(FFFB518);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="40" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 32 — Idle State]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(WKRLVL0)XIC(M0899),XIC(WKRLVL1)]XIO(WKRLVL2)XIO(WKRLVL5)MOV(100,R00812);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="41" Type="N">
