<Routine Name="DISPB1" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Display Bus 1 Control Block]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 4 — ) The Display Board will display negative numbers, so we check to see if the value in the Global data register is negative. If it is then we get it's absolute value which is done by subtracting it from zero. Then set an internal bit indicating a negative number will be displayed. ) Since the 9030 display driver can only handle 4 digits we must make sure that the value to be displayed must not exceed 9999. If it does then we clamp it at 9999.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALW_ON)LES(R03241,0)OTE(M3489);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 4 — ) The Display Board will display negative numbers, so we check to see if the value in the Global data register is negative. If it is then we get it's absolute value which is done by subtracting it from zero. Then set an internal bit indicating a negative number will be displayed. ) Since the 9030 display driver can only handle 4 digits we must make sure that the value to be displayed must not exceed 9999. If it does then we clamp it at 9999.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALW_ON)SUB(0,R03241,R03241);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 6 — Convert value in the Global Data register to BCD.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALW_ON)MOV(9999,R03241);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 8 — Calculate the number of bits the Minus Sign mask has to be shifted. The formula to calculate is number of display digits - 1 4]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALW_ON)TOD(R03241,R03244);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 10 — Take the Minus Sign code 0AH and shift it in the Display Mask by the number of bits from the above calculation.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(M3489)SUB(R03245,1,R03246);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 10 — Take the Minus Sign code 0AH and shift it in the Display Mask by the number of bits from the above calculation.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(M3489)MUL(R03246,4,R03246);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 10 — Take the Minus Sign code 0AH and shift it in the Display Mask by the number of bits from the above calculation.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(M3489)MOV(R03246,R03247);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 10 — Take the Minus Sign code 0AH and shift it in the Display Mask by the number of bits from the above calculation.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(M3489)OTE(CONT_DISPB1_10);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 12 — If the Value to be displayed is a negative number then OR its BCD register with the Negative number Mask.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(CONT_DISPB1_10)XIC(ALW_OFF)SHL(R03247,R03246,R03248);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 14 — If the Display Blank Dashes bit is set then clear the Global Display register and mask in dashes. Reset the Display Bland Dashes bit to be set for the next display rountine call.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(M3489)OR(R03244,R03248,R03244);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 16 — Load the Global Data register into the display data bus. Then Load the Addr. Bus with correct display address.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(M3490)MOV(0,R03244);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 16 — Load the Global Data register into the display data bus. Then Load the Addr. Bus with correct display address.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(M3490)OR(R03244,0,R03244);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 16 — Load the Global Data register into the display data bus. Then Load the Addr. Bus with correct display address.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(M3490)OTU(M3490);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 18 — All data must be set with the strobe line off. Once the data is loaded set the strobe bit, and use DO_IO to update all Data and Address I/O. Then clear the strobe bit and use DO_IO to update.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALW_ON)NEQ(R03244,0)OTE(Q0737);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 18 — All data must be set with the strobe line off. Once the data is loaded set the strobe bit, and use DO_IO to update all Data and Address I/O. Then clear the strobe bit and use DO_IO to update.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALW_ON)EQU(R03244,0)OTU(Q0737);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 18 — All data must be set with the strobe line off. Once the data is loaded set the strobe bit, and use DO_IO to update all Data and Address I/O. Then clear the strobe bit and use DO_IO to update.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALW_ON)XIC(Q0737)OTE(Q0757);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 18 — All data must be set with the strobe line off. Once the data is loaded set the strobe bit, and use DO_IO to update all Data and Address I/O. Then clear the strobe bit and use DO_IO to update.]]>
