<Routine Name="INCDEC" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[IncDec Bounds Control Block]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 5 — ) ********** Inc / Dec / Bounds Check Routine * IDBUse30.inc ****************************************************** This routine performs the following functions: 1. Decrements or increments input value by 1, 10, or a user defined amount. This is controlled by flags in the input table. 2. Bounds checks input value against a minimum and maximum value in the input table. Result will be greater than or equal to minimum and less than or equal to maximum limits. 3. Sets underflow or overflow flags in result table. 4. Returns validated result and flags to input table for use by main program. *********************************************************************** Local Working Register Usage: (Passed to this routine by the caller) ============================= Note: Because the 90/30 does not hav… If the dec or inc is active, set the amount to add or subtract accordingly.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALW_ON)COP(R00411,R00401,4);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 5 — ) ********** Inc / Dec / Bounds Check Routine * IDBUse30.inc ****************************************************** This routine performs the following functions: 1. Decrements or increments input value by 1, 10, or a user defined amount. This is controlled by flags in the input table. 2. Bounds checks input value against a minimum and maximum value in the input table. Result will be greater than or equal to minimum and less than or equal to maximum limits. 3. Sets underflow or overflow flags in result table. 4. Returns validated result and flags to input table for use by main program. *********************************************************************** Local Working Register Usage: (Passed to this routine by the caller) ============================= Note: Because the 90/30 does not hav… If the dec or inc is active, set the amount to add or subtract accordingly.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALW_ON)NEQ(R00401,0)OTE(T0001);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 5 — ) ********** Inc / Dec / Bounds Check Routine * IDBUse30.inc ****************************************************** This routine performs the following functions: 1. Decrements or increments input value by 1, 10, or a user defined amount. This is controlled by flags in the input table. 2. Bounds checks input value against a minimum and maximum value in the input table. Result will be greater than or equal to minimum and less than or equal to maximum limits. 3. Sets underflow or overflow flags in result table. 4. Returns validated result and flags to input table for use by main program. *********************************************************************** Local Working Register Usage: (Passed to this routine by the caller) ============================= Note: Because the 90/30 does not hav… If the dec or inc is active, set the amount to add or subtract accordingly.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ALW_ON)EQU(R00401,0)OTU(T0001);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Description>
