<Routine Name="PLINE" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[PLine Wedge Control Block]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Description>
<![CDATA[GE Rung 4 — ) PLine.inc Passline / Wedge On some systems the mill pass line can be adjusted by opening or closing a wedge that moves the roll stack. Open means the roll gap gets larger and close means the roll gap gets smaller. The operator needs to know the current pass line in order to set it. Based on the wedge position, the calibration settings, and the roll diameters, the passline position can be displayed. Required hardware / signals: - A position transducer to determine the wedge position. - A display to show the current pass line. - A full open detection device. - Manual control to open and close the wedge. - A means to enter the backup roll and work roll diameters. - A calibration screen to assist the calibration procedure. How it works: The position transducer detects the horizontal position… Load zero into the Passline seek register. When in the OnLine sequence load the target position into this register.]]>
</Description>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(HYDSRUN),XIC(ONOFS2)XIO(SDFORCE),XIC(ONOFS6),XIC(ONOFS8)]XIO(MILLTRN)XIO(FRNTFRC)XIO(REARFRC)XIC(CTRBLON)OTE(M1037);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
